<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mubariz Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1724</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mubariz Khan was a Mughal noble and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> who was appointed by the court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> to oppose the growing independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-jah-i">Nizam-ul-Mulk</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. He was defeated and killed by Nizam-ul-Mulk at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shakar-kheda">Battle of Shakar Kheda</a> in October 1724, a victory that founded Hyderabad State.</p></div>
